<tool id="gemma_kinship" name="GEMMA Kinship" version="0.98.6">
  <description>Compute kinship matrix using GEMMA</description>
  <requirements>
    <container type="docker">voluture2721/galaxy-gemma:0.98.6</container>
  </requirements>
  <command detect_errors="exit_code">
    <![CDATA[
    mkdir -p output &&
    gemma -g '$geno_input' 
          -p '$pheno_input' 
          -gk 
          -o kinship_matrix
    ]]>
  </command>
  <inputs>
    <param name="geno_input" type="data" format="txt,tabular" label="Genotype file (geno.txt.gz)" />
    <param name="pheno_input" type="data" format="txt,tabular" label="Phenotype file (pheno.txt)" />
  </inputs>
  <outputs>
    <data name="output_kinship" format="txt" from_work_dir="output/kinship_matrix.cXX.txt" label="GEMMA Kinship Matrix" />
  </outputs>
  <tests>
    <test>
      <param name="geno_input" value="mouse_hs1940.geno.txt.gz" />
      <param name="pheno_input" value="mouse_hs1940.pheno.txt" />
      <output name="output_kinship" file="mouse_hs1940.cXX.txt" compare="sim_size" />
    </test>
  </tests>
  <help>
    <![CDATA[
**GEMMA Kinship Matrix Computation**

This tool computes a kinship matrix using GEMMA (Genome-wide Efficient Mixed Model Association).

Command equivalent:
docker run -v $(pwd)/example:/data -w /data --rm galaxy-gemma:0.98.6 \
  gemma -g mouse_hs1940.geno.txt.gz -p mouse_hs1940.pheno.txt -gk -o mouse_hs1940

For more information, see the GEMMA manual: https://github.com/genetics-statistics/GEMMA
    ]]>
  </help>
</tool>